@startuml selma_compilation_pipeline
' ============================================================
' Selma — Hermetic Compilation / CG-IR Pipeline
' Source:  SPECIFICATION.md §2.4, §2.6, §2.7, §2.8, §2.9, §3.4, §3.5
'          User_Stories.md S-05, S-21..S-24, S-27, S-31
' C4:      Hermetic Compiler → Compiled Rules Adapter → cgir_store
'          (read-lock on directive_store; conflict_resolver at compile)
' Contract: 8.2.4
'
' Invariants:
'   · hermetic frozen_env boundary
'   · any gate fail → no partial CG-IR
'   · content-addressed SHA-256 snapshot identity
'   · compiled_at excluded from snapshot hash (S-23)
'   · policy_doctrine.yaml never required at runtime (AA-02)
' ============================================================

title Selma — Hermetic Compilation / CG-IR Pipeline\n<size:12><i>All-or-nothing publish · content-addressed · no runtime policy dependency</i></size>

!include ./common/sm_styles.puml

[*] --> Requested : <b>compile request</b>\ntrigger: directive change | CI/CD\nrequest_id tracked

state "Requested" as Requested #B9770E : queued · dedup by\n(graph version + frozen_env)
state "Queued" as Queued #B9770E : FIFO · writer-preference\nblocks new readers when\nwrite pending (§3.4)
state "Acquire\nRead Lock" as AcquireReadLock #B9770E : concurrent compiles OK\nblocks on write lock
state "Schema\nValidate" as SchemaValidate #1B7A6E : JSON Schema Draft-07\nstructural projection
state "Complexity\nValidate" as ComplexityValidate #1B7A6E : AST walk\ndepth≤32 · nodes≤256\nwidth≤64 · regex≤4096\nmetadata≤16384 B
state "Portability\nValidate" as PortabilityValidate #1B7A6E : RE2 · IEEE 754 finite\nUTC-Z · NFC strings\nflags {i,m,s} only
state "Discriminator\nValidate" as DiscriminatorValidate #1B7A6E : evaluator_type ↔ config\nAST discriminator (§2.9)
state "Lineage DAG\nValidate" as LineageValidate #1B7A6E : acyclicity · depth≤64\nparent existence\noperation consistency
state "Hash Nodes" as HashNodes #1B7A6E : semantic_hash +\npresentation_hash → node_hash\nincremental reuse
state "Hash Edges" as HashEdges #1B7A6E : edge_hash =\nSHA-256(source, target)
state "Conflict\nMap" as ConflictMap #1B7A6E : resolve_conflict mapping\nprecedence §2.15
state "Snapshot\nHash" as SnapshotHash #1B7A6E : cg_ir_snapshot_hash =\nSHA-256(sorted node_hashes +\nsorted edge_hashes +\nprovenance)\n**compiled_at excluded**
state "Policy Runtime\nProhibition Assert" as PolicyAssert #1B7A6E : AA-02 · policy absent\nfrom runtime data paths
state "Publish CAS" as Publish #2C6E49 : immutable snapshot\ndedup if hash exists
state "Release Lock\n(Success)" as ReleaseLockOk #2C6E49 : read lock released\nafter successful publish
state "Release Lock\n(Abort)" as ReleaseLockFail #A93226 : read lock released\nafter gate failure
state "Completed" as Completed #2C6E49 : snapshot live\ninspections may pin hash
state "Failed" as Failed #A93226 : **no partial CG-IR**\nDirective Graph unchanged\naudit entry only

Requested --> Queued
Queued --> AcquireReadLock
AcquireReadLock --> SchemaValidate : lock granted
AcquireReadLock --> Queued : blocked · retry FIFO

SchemaValidate --> ComplexityValidate : PASS
SchemaValidate --> Failed : FAIL · SchemaError

ComplexityValidate --> PortabilityValidate : PASS
ComplexityValidate --> Failed : FAIL · ComplexityError

PortabilityValidate --> DiscriminatorValidate : PASS
PortabilityValidate --> Failed : FAIL · PortabilityError

DiscriminatorValidate --> LineageValidate : PASS
DiscriminatorValidate --> Failed : FAIL · DiscriminatorError

LineageValidate --> HashNodes : PASS\nlineage_validation recorded
LineageValidate --> Failed : FAIL · LineageError

HashNodes --> HashEdges
HashEdges --> ConflictMap
ConflictMap --> SnapshotHash : pairs mapped\n(unresolved → conflict artifact meta;\ncross-lineage advisory only)

SnapshotHash --> PolicyAssert
PolicyAssert --> Publish : PASS
PolicyAssert --> Failed : FAIL · ArchitecturalAuditError AA-02

Publish --> ReleaseLockOk
ReleaseLockOk --> Completed
Completed --> [*]

Failed --> ReleaseLockFail : always release lock
ReleaseLockFail --> [*]

note left of AcquireReadLock
  **Concurrency (§3.4)**
  · Compilation = read lock only
  · Directive mutation = exclusive write lock
  · Writer-preference FIFO
  · No write-lock-while-awaiting-compile
  · Identical content → same hash → no-op dedup
end note

note right of SnapshotHash
  **Hermetic boundary (§2.7)**
  frozen_env pins engine, toolchain,
  OS hash, model/prompt/decoder (if any),
  confidence_severity_cap_threshold.
  frozen_env_hash excludes itself.
end note

note bottom of Publish
  **Immutability**
  Once published, CG-IR is never mutated.
  Further directive changes produce a **new**
  snapshot under a new content hash.
  Storage: cgir_store (CAS) via Compiled Rules Adapter.
  Success and abort lock-release paths are
  distinct states (no ambiguous dual exit).
end note

@enduml
